Researching each creator's public bio, products, and documented strategy to build accurate playbook entries.
{"tdinh_me":{"plays":[{"id":"tdinh_me-1","emoji":"🚀","title":"Feature-as-Marketing Ship Loop","description":"Tony's TypingMind growth came from tweeting every new feature as it shipped — his entire marketing strategy was changelog posts that doubled as sales triggers.","action":"Ship one visible product improvement, record a 30-second screen demo, and post it with a one-line pain point it solves plus a link to try it.","frequency":"Daily"},{"id":"tdinh_me-2","emoji":"📊","title":"Revenue Milestone Transparency","description":"He posts MRR snapshots and milestone timelines ($1K → $10K → $22K in 7 days) to build trust and FOMO, while crediting years of daily coding as the real unfair advantage.","action":"Share a screenshot of a real revenue or user milestone with a short timeline of what you shipped to get there — include one failed attempt for credibility.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"tdinh_me-3","emoji":"🎯","title":"Weekend MVP Launch","description":"TypingMind went from ChatGPT API announcement (Mar 1) to live MVP (Mar 6) by solving his own daily annoyances — slow typing, forced re-login — not chasing trends.","action":"Pick one personal workflow pain, register a domain, build a minimal static MVP over a weekend, and announce it the moment payments work.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"tdinh_me-4","emoji":"💬","title":"High-Intent DM Outreach","description":"During Black Magic growth he DM'd ~20 people daily — new followers and engagers — turning conversations into beta users and organic word-of-mouth.","action":"Each morning DM 10–20 people who engaged with your last post; thank them, ask one question about their workflow, and offer early access if relevant.","frequency":"Daily"},{"id":"tdinh_me-5","emoji":"📬","title":"Owned-Audience Newsletter Bridge","description":"After Twitter API pricing threatened Black Magic, he pushed followers to his Substack newsletter as a platform-independent distribution channel he controls.","action":"Republish your best X thread or product update as a newsletter issue with one exclusive detail not posted on X, and link it from your bio.","frequency":"Weekly"}],"hooks":["My weekend project is now available: {productURL} — I was so annoyed by {painPoint}, so I built {oneLineSolution}.","First sale on {paymentProvider} 🥳🥳🥳","$10K revenue! 🥳 — started as a weekend side project — MVP released on {date} — {dayByDayRevenueTimeline}","Every time I add a new feature, I tweet about it — and that's my entire marketing strategy.","They say I make ${MRR}/month just by pure luck and posting my MRR on Twitter 🙃 I'll ignore them and have my {X} years of GitHub graph printed on my wall.","Launch report for {product}! 🥳 🏆 #{rank} Product of the Day — Added ~${amount} revenue — Thank you all!!!"],"angles":["Solve-your-own-pain AI developer tools","Build in public with raw revenue numbers","Fast-shipping weekend MVPs on new API launches","Developer humor and relatable coding memes","Product Hunt launches after organic X traction","Unfair-advantage transparency (audience + speed + product sense)"]},"dannypostma":{"plays":[{"id":"dannypostma-1","emoji":"📸","title":"Visual-First Product Drop","description":"HeadshotPro and Deep Agency launched with stunning before/after AI headshot grids and model photos that did the selling before any explanation — visuals drove millions of impressions.","action":"Create a 4-image grid showing dramatic before/after results from your AI tool, post with zero setup text, then follow with a thread explaining the product.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"dannypostma-2","emoji":"🧵","title":"Launch Thread Funnel","description":"Major launches (Deep Agency, HeadshotPro) used multi-tweet threads starting with a hook visual, then stepping through features, pricing, and CTA — classic solopreneur launch playbook.","action":"Draft a 5–8 tweet thread: hook image → problem → demo video → pricing → link. Schedule tweets 2 minutes apart on launch day.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"dannypostma-3","emoji":"🔍","title":"SEO Landing Page Army","description":"HeadshotPro ranks via programmatic SEO pages (e.g. ai-headshot-generator) linked from his bio — organic search complements viral X spikes.","action":"Build 3–5 keyword-specific landing pages for your core use case, link the top performer in your X bio, and tweet one page when you ship a related feature.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"dannypostma-4","emoji":"🤖","title":"AI-Accelerated Solo Build","description":"He publicly embraced AI doing 80% of his coding, positioning himself as a one-person studio shipping enterprise-grade AI products from Ho Chi Minh City.","action":"Record a screen capture of you building a feature with AI assistance, post it with an honest estimate of human vs. AI contribution, and link the result.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"dannypostma-5","emoji":"👀","title":"Pre-Launch Tease","description":"Deep Agency teased AI models that 'do not exist' days before launch — building anticipation and letting the audience spread the mystery.","action":"Post a teaser image or demo of your unreleased product with 'coming soon' and a waitlist link — no full explanation until launch day.","frequency":"Monthly"}],"hooks":["Both of these models do not exist. You can hire them on {productURL} once it's live.","These headshots? Made entirely by AI. 😎 Introducing {productName}: {oneLineValueProp}. Details in the next tweets ↓","After MONTHS of work, it's finally here! 🚀 {productName}: {tagline}. Full explanation in the next few tweets ↓","You're only successful because you have a large following. BS. Here's how you can do the same with 0 followers 🧵👇","AI is doing 80% of my coding – the future looks brighter than ever! 🤩","> open LinkedIn > cringe > close LinkedIn"],"angles":["Stunning AI-generated visual demos as primary marketing","Solopreneur lifestyle from Southeast Asia","Anti-corporate casual tone and observational humor","Multi-product AI studio (HeadshotPro, Deep Agency, etc.)","Distribution-without-audience myth-busting threads","Tech culture commentary and contrarian takes"]},"arvidkahl":{"plays":[{"id":"arvidkahl-1","emoji":"🎙️","title":"Ecosystem Data Authority","description":"With Podscan he posts podcast industry stats — episode counts, growth projections, pandemic-era comparisons — positioning himself as the data source for podcast marketing decisions.","action":"Pull one proprietary or aggregated stat from your product database, visualize it as a chart screenshot, and post with a single actionable takeaway for founders.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"arvidkahl-2","emoji":"🤝","title":"Kindness Amplification","description":"His bio promise — 'raising all the boats with kindness' — shows in quote-tweets that add nuance, celebrate others' wins, and avoid dunking; he builds reputation through generosity.","action":"Quote-tweet one indie hacker's milestone or insight with a genuine 2–3 sentence addition that makes their point sharper — never snark.","frequency":"Daily"},{"id":"arvidkahl-3","emoji":"📖","title":"Bootstrapped SaaS Teaching","description":"Author of Zero to Sold and The Embedded Entrepreneur, he converts lived experience (FeedbackPanda exit) into frameworks founders can apply — books, blog (tbf.link), and podcast (tbf.fm).","action":"Share one tactical lesson from your exit or current build as a standalone post — no thread needed — and link your blog only when asked.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"arvidkahl-4","emoji":"🔧","title":"Build-in-Public Engineering","description":"He posts real technical struggles (500GB full-text search, Laravel discovery moments) and invites the community to help — vulnerability builds trust and surfaces solutions.","action":"Post a genuine technical blocker you're facing tonight, tag no vendors, and ask 'what would you use?' — reply thoughtfully to every suggestion.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"arvidkahl-5","emoji":"💡","title":"Pragmatic Product Takes","description":"Recurring theme: 'The goal is to build a business. Not to play startup.' — he contrasts sustainable bootstrapping with performative founder culture.","action":"Write one post contrasting a business-building decision you made vs. the 'startup playbook' alternative, with the revenue or customer impact.","frequency":"Monthly"}],"hooks":["The goal is to build a business. Not to play startup.","Stats update! Since {product} tracks {dataset}, we can reliably project {trend}. Don't sleep on {medium}.","When someone signs up to your SaaS, grab their email domain, get a summary from {tool}, have an LLM generate the best starting config. First impression: magical.","If a tire company can publish a globally recognized restaurant guide, then you're allowed to work on your completely unrelated side projects.","Cancelled my {service} account today — I was pleasantly surprised when they offered me a refund. That's EXTREMELY customer-friendly.","Okay call me a noob, but I just had a life-changing experience with {technology}. After ~2 minutes of configuring, I have {impressiveResult}. WHAT?! 🤣"],"angles":["Bootstrapped SaaS wisdom from a real exit (FeedbackPanda)","Podcast ecosystem data and industry trend analysis","Kindness-forward community building and amplification","Long-form nuanced commentary on culture and technology","Transparent building of Podscan and Podline in public","Pragmatic engineering and anti-performative-startup framing"]},"yongfook":{"plays":[{"id":"yongfook-1","emoji":"🐻","title":"Ship-More Portfolio Honesty","description":"Pinned post: 20+ projects shipped over 20 years, only Bannerbear makes real money at ~$81K MRR — he normalizes failure volume as the path to one winner.","action":"Post your project scorecard (shipped / making money / failed / in progress) with a '🚀 So... ship more' closer — update it annually.","frequency":"Yearly"},{"id":"yongfook-2","emoji":"📈","title":"Salary and MRR Chart Posts","description":"His 'salary over the last 20 years' chart went viral (949K quotes) — visual career arcs make abstract bootstrapping tangible and shareable.","action":"Create a simple line or bar chart of your income trajectory (job → side project → full-time indie) and post it with zero thread — let the image speak.","frequency":"Yearly"},{"id":"yongfook-3","emoji":"😂","title":"Meme-as-Market-Commentary","description":"GPT-wrapper panic memes, satirical engagement-bait threads, and UI parody posts consistently outperform his straight product tweets — humor is his top-of-funnel.","action":"When a platform shift threatens your space (new GPT feature, Apple UI trend), post a meme or satirical one-liner within 24 hours — ride the news cycle.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"yongfook-4","emoji":"🛠️","title":"Growth-Over-Cost Pragmatism","description":"When devs suggested migrating Bannerbear to save server costs, he replied he's optimizing for growth not saving a few hundred dollars — anti-pedantry positioning.","action":"Share a real infra cost number ($X/month at $Y MRR) and explicitly state what you're NOT optimizing for — shuts down unhelpful advice and signals confidence.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"yongfook-5","emoji":"🚀","title":"MVP Origin Story Posts","description":"'This grew into a $12 billion business. Ship your MVP.' — he pairs humble early screenshots of famous products with a one-line bootstrapping sermon.","action":"Find a scrappy early screenshot of a now-huge product in your niche, post it with 'Ship your MVP' and optionally tie it to something you're building.","frequency":"Monthly"}],"hooks":["🚀 In the last 20+ years I shipped {N} projects 🐻 1 of those makes decent money ({product}) 📉 The other {N} failed 🚀 So... ship more","My salary over the last 20 years","I'm a dev. My app makes ${MRR}/mo. I just revealed that my server costs are ${cost}/mo. I'm not looking to save a few hundred bucks. I'm looking to grow my business.","AI startups building on GPT realizing that new GPT basically replaces their product offering.","This grew into a $12 billion business. Ship your MVP.","Taylor Swift will make $10 million *on each day* of her upcoming tour. But the crazy thing? Most people are using Notion entirely wrong. Here's 10 ways to bootstrap your AI startup to $8 MRR. 🧵👀"],"angles":["Brutally honest project failure rates and 'ship more' mantra","Bannerbear/Browserbear API-product bootstrapping","Viral memes and satire about AI, VC, and tech culture","Income and career trajectory visual storytelling","Anti-optimization pragmatism for growing SaaS","Singapore-based indie founder lifestyle and travel observations"]},"hnshah":{"plays":[{"id":"hnshah-1","emoji":"⏳","title":"Long-Game Principle Posts","description":"Pinned 'The long game is less crowded' encapsulates his content — short, timeless SaaS wisdom drawn from 20+ years building Crazy Egg, KISSmetrics, and Nira.","action":"Write one sentence that reframes a common startup anxiety (burnout, competition, pivoting) through a 10-year lens — no product pitch.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"hnshah-2","emoji":"📚","title":"Curated Resource Threads","description":"His 'never ending thread of the very best online content for early stage startups' became a bookmark magnet — he aggregates value instead of only creating it.","action":"Start or update a pinned thread of 10–20 links (articles, tools, podcasts) you genuinely recommend for early-stage founders — add one new link monthly.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"hnshah-3","emoji":"🎬","title":"Pop-Culture Founder Analogies","description":"Breaking Bad as a co-founder story thread (4.2M quotes) — he maps entertainment narratives onto startup dynamics to make business lessons visceral and shareable.","action":"Pick a popular show, movie, or clip and write 3 scenes mapped to founder lessons (co-founder conflict, execution vs. planning) — post as a short thread.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"hnshah-4","emoji":"✂️","title":"Clip-and-Commentary Distribution","description":"He shares clips of others (Sam Altman on first 100 users, startup humor videos) with a one-line framing insight — low production, high reach.","action":"Find a 30–60 second clip from a podcast or video relevant to your audience, post it with one sentence of your take — not a summary, a perspective.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"hnshah-5","emoji":"📰","title":"SaaS Weekly Newsletter Funnel","description":"hiten.com and SaaS Weekly newsletter extend X reach into owned email — his bio points to durable content beyond the timeline.","action":"Turn your best-performing X post of the week into a 3-paragraph newsletter blurb with one extra insight, and tease it on X with 'deeper dive in this week's SaaS Weekly.'","frequency":"Weekly"}],"hooks":["The long game is less crowded.","Opportunities unfold as you execute. Not as you whiteboard.","Don't be the idea guy or gal. Be the execution person. It pays a lot more.","You don't burn out from working too hard. You burn out from doing work that doesn't matter, surrounded by people who don't notice.","Breaking Bad is a co-founder story disguised as a drug-dealing story. Here are the best example scenes and what you can learn from them.","This is a never ending thread of the very best online content and resources for early stage startups."],"angles":["20-year SaaS operator principles that endure across cycles","Startup psychology and founder mental health","Pop-culture and media analogies for business lessons","Curated resource curation for early-stage founders","Execution-over-ideation framing","Product-led growth and SaaS metrics wisdom from Crazy Egg/KISSmetrics era"]},"damengchen":{"plays":[{"id":"damengchen-1","emoji":"🎬","title":"Ship-and-Demo Feature Posts","description":"Pinned tweet pattern: screen recording of a just-shipped feature (NPS auto-routing on Testimonial.to) with emoji-labeled user flows — product-led content marketing.","action":"Record a 45-second demo of today's shipped feature, label user paths with emoji (🟢🟡🔴), and post 'Just shipped {feature} in {productURL}.'","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"damengchen-2","emoji":"📊","title":"MRR Milestone Broadcast","description":"He tweeted approaching $1K MRR which attracted Andrew Gazdecki as a customer; milestone posts create social proof and attract high-value signups organically.","action":"When within 10% of a round MRR number, post 'Almost at ${target} MRR with {product}' — include one growth tactic that got you there.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"damengchen-3","emoji":"🔄","title":"Product-Led Growth Loop","description":"Testimonial's wall-of-love pages display the Testimonial logo, creating a viral loop: collect testimonial → publish wall → visitors sign up → repeat.","action":"Ensure your product leaves a tasteful branded artifact on customer output (embed, watermark, 'powered by'); screenshot a customer wall and post the loop diagram.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"damengchen-4","emoji":"🌙","title":"Night-Shift Builder Narrative","description":"Quit Cisco after 4 failed projects; grew Testimonial on nights/weekends while kids slept — he shares the parenting + indie grind reality, not just wins.","action":"Post one honest snapshot of your build schedule (playground support tickets, post-bedtime coding) when you ship something meaningful — relatability drives engagement.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"damengchen-5","emoji":"🧩","title":"Portfolio Product Expansion","description":"PDF.ai spun out of Testimonial customer pain; he runs multiple small products (Testimonial, PDF.ai, StreetInterview.ai, Mailcheep) from shared code and audience.","action":"When an existing customer reveals an adjacent pain, scope a minimal new product reusing 80% of your stack, launch on Product Hunt, and cross-promote to your base.","frequency":"Quarterly"}],"hooks":["Just shipped {feature} in {productURL}. {emoji} {userType} → {action} 🟡 {userType} → {action} 🔴 {userType} → {action}","I quit my job and put my family at risk since we live in the very expensive SF Bay Area. {N} months later, I hit $100k ARR with {N} projects.","I was once in a job interview, and the person asked me to {question}. I answered with {simpleAnswer}, then I got rejected. 🤷‍♂️","Oh hey @{bigCompany}, if you're considering wasting $10 million on Google Ads for '{keyword}' keywords, you know you have another option 🤭","You almost never hear a VC-backed startup share bad news. Everything is great until the day before they announce they're shutting down.","My wife works a 9-5. She is paid well... I'm starting to wonder: is entrepreneurship over-glorified? 🤔"],"angles":["Engineer-turned-indie-hacker with family and Bay Area constraints","Product-led growth and viral wall-of-love loops","Multiple small bets portfolio (Testimonial, PDF.ai, etc.)","MRR milestones and transparent revenue journey","Relatable tech-industry humor and cultural observations","Night-and-weekend shipping while parenting"]},"levelsio":{"plays":[{"id":"levelsio-1","emoji":"💰","title":"Live MRR Bio Dashboard","description":"His X bio lists every product with current MRR ($100K/m PhotoAI, $44K/m RemoteOK, etc.) — updated regularly, it functions as a real-time portfolio scoreboard and credibility signal.","action":"Add current MRR next to each product in your bio; update the numbers monthly and tweet when any product crosses a round milestone.","frequency":"Monthly"},{"id":"levelsio-2","emoji":"🏝️","title":"Nomad-Life Observation Posts","description":"Travel posts (Dubai solar farm, Barcelona garbage trucks, Portugal-Brazil dynamics) routinely hit millions of impressions — curiosity-driven content unrelated to his products fuels top-of-funnel reach.","action":"When traveling, film or photograph something surprising about local infrastructure, culture, or tech — post a one-line observation with no product mention.","frequency":"Weekly"},{"id":"levelsio-3","emoji":"🎂","title":"Ship-More Failure Math","description":"Pinned philosophy: >95% of 70+ projects failed, ~5% hit rate — 'So...ship more' — he uses volume statistics to normalize failure and encourage builders.","action":"Post your hit-rate math (projects tried / projects profitable) with a cake or chart image and end with '🚀 So...ship more.'","frequency":"Yearly"},{"id":"levelsio-4","emoji":"📸","title":"AI Product Demo-as-Content","description":"PhotoAI, InteriorAI, and similar products market themselves through stunning before/after AI outputs posted directly to X — the demo is the ad.","action":"Generate your product's most impressive output on a trending subject (celebrity, news event, viral aesthetic) and post the result with one line and a link.","frequency":"Daily"},{"id":"levelsio-5","emoji":"🏆","title":"Community Competition Engine","description":"Vibe Jam 2026 — $25K prizes, 1000 submissions, sponsor integrations — he uses competitions to engage builders and create months of content from one event.","action":"Launch or sponsor a themed build competition with a clear prize, post judging updates and winner announcements as multi-day content arcs.","frequency":"Quarterly"}],"hooks":["🍰 Only {hits} out of {total}+ projects I ever did made money and grew 📉 >{failRate}% of everything I ever did failed 📈 My hit rate is only about ~{rate}% 🚀 So...ship more","📸 {product} ${MRR}/m 🛰 {product} ${MRR}/m — (bio-style portfolio listing)","Today I randomly discovered {place} has {surprisingThing}???","What's crazy when you read about {company} is you realize {industryLeader} are essentially dropshippers","Guys....are you thinking what I am thinking?","🏋️ I made a {funnyETF} with only companies with CEOs that {criteria}. It outperforms the S&P500 by {X}%!"],"angles":["Radical revenue transparency across a multi-product portfolio","Nomad lifestyle and global travel curiosity posts","AI product demos (PhotoAI, InteriorAI) as native advertising","High-volume posting mixing business, culture, and random observations","Ship-more volume philosophy and failure normalization","Community events and competitions (Vibe Jam) as engagement engines"]}}
